<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="003" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Record the credential decision with evidence</title>
    <phase>0 Spike</phase>
    <gate>002 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Decision documentation; no code changes.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Synthesis of recorded evidence into a decision record.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches .claude/adr/ — main-session only per the sub-agent write boundary.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <tags>documentation,auth,adr</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Convert the spike evidence into a recorded credential decision — MI-FIC confirmed, or pivot to the ADR-028 A4 sanctioned alternative (Key Vault certificate). Update design.md §6 Phase 0 and ADR-028's A4 adoption status.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Apply the CLAUDE.md §6.5 ADR conflict discipline.</role>
  <goal>A decision record a future reader cannot re-open without new evidence, plus an ADR-028 note reflecting adoption status.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design.md §6 makes Phase 0 the decision gate. ADR-028 A4 already specifies the target shape; this records whether our chain actually satisfies it. §1.2 explains why recording the decision matters: the last three audits closed this question on an unrecorded premise.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/design.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/002-spike-results.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="002" status="pending">Spike evidence</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: record the decision only. Do NOT begin implementation in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: if the spike failed, the fallback is a Key Vault certificate — NEVER a retained secret as the permanent answer. E-3 is transitional and time-boxed to this project.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: .claude/ edits are main-session only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ADR amendment, decision records</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/RESEARCH-FINDINGS.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/TENANCY-AND-CREDENTIALS.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Summarise the spike outcome against each must-prove item from spec §4 Phase 0.</step>
    <step>State the decision: MI-FIC adopted, or pivot to certificate with reasons.</step>
    <step>Update design.md §6 Phase 0 row to DONE with the outcome.</step>
    <step>Add an adoption-status line to ADR-028 Amendment A4.</step>
    <step>If pivoting: re-open the certificate provisioning work that TENANCY-AND-CREDENTIALS recorded as dropped, explicitly.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Evidence is ambiguous or intermittent — STOP. Do not record a decision on a flaky result; that is how the original false premise survived.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/003-credential-decision.md</output>
    <output type="modify">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/design.md</output>
    <output type="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The decision is stated unambiguously with linked evidence for each must-prove item.</criterion>
    <criterion>design.md §6 Phase 0 reflects the outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADR-028 A4 carries an adoption-status note.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: if pivoted, the certificate provisioning work is explicitly re-opened rather than silently assumed absent.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <completion date="2026-08-20" rigor="FULL" rigor-override-reason="POML authored STANDARD; overridden UP because tags include auth. Step 9.5 gates still skip -- documentation-only.">
      DECISION RECORDED: MI-FIC ADOPTED. Option B (Key Vault certificate) NOT taken; it remains the sanctioned
      alternative where the same-tenant rule cannot hold. Certificate provisioning work correctly stays dropped --
      TENANCY-AND-CREDENTIALS recorded it as such and this decision does not re-open it.

      Every Phase-0 must-prove item is linked to a reproducible observation rather than an argument, because an
      unrecorded premise is exactly how the last three audits closed this question wrongly.

      TWO ITEMS RECORDED AS NOT PROVEN rather than folded into a pass:
        - Power BI: DEFERRED by owner 2026-08-20 (DEF-001 / #804). Separate credential, no OBO path reads it.
        - Model 2 cross-tenant FIC shape: STILL OPEN, owed by customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 (§9.2).
          A4's own same-tenant constraint means a cross-tenant FIC may be structurally impossible, in which case
          Model 2 needs the KV-certificate alternative. Neither gates a dev-only Model 1 rollout, and recording
          them as open is the point -- a future reader must not read this as having settled Model 2.

      ADR-028 A4 updated with an ADOPTION STATUS block (accepted-on-reasoning -> verified-on-the-wire).

      ALSO CORRECTED A4 ITSELF: its "Preferred wiring" section recommends Microsoft.Identity.Web's declarative
      ordered ClientCredentials JSON, which finding E4' shows is UNUSABLE in this codebase (zero
      EnableTokenAcquisition / ITokenAcquisition / IDownstreamApi / ClientCredentials in any .cs;
      AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApi is inbound-only; Spaarke.Dataverse has no Identity.Web reference). Left in place
      as accurate general Microsoft guidance but annotated, because a reader following it literally would
      configure the JSON, see no effect, and reasonably conclude MI-FIC does not work here. The consequence is
      load-bearing: the ordered fallback must be BUILT (task 021), not inherited.

      Also recorded: what would legitimately re-open the decision (4 concrete conditions), and the distinguishable
      failure modes -- managed_identity_unreachable_network (no MI) / managed_identity_request_failed (wrong
      identity) / AADSTS7000215 (wrong-or-stale secret, opaque) / AADSTS70021 (FIC propagation, RETRY FIRST).

      No escalation trigger fired -- evidence was consistent and non-flaky across repeated runs.

      CROSS-PROJECT: open PR #801 edits this project's design.md at the sequencing bullet (line ~367) where our
      branch already carries the same correction in different wording. Same substance, textual conflict at merge.
      Flagged on the PR; this task's edits are in §6 and do not worsen it.

      Full record: notes/decisions/003-credential-decision.md
    </completion>
  </notes>
</task>
